.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pons-scan 1  "scan "
.SH NAME
pons\-scan \- Scan a file or directory and report findings
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpons scan\fR [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-rule\fR] [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-speculative\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\-skips\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-language\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a file or directory and report findings
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<FAIL_ON>\fR
Exit 1 if any non\-speculative finding meets or exceeds this severity
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
info
.IP \(bu 2
warn
.IP \(bu 2
error
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]
Output format. `human` is the default; `json` and `sarif` emit the machine\-readable envelopes from PLAN Appendices G and E
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
sarif
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
TOML configuration. Defaults to `pons.toml` at the scan root
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR \fI<RULE>\fR
Select rule IDs; repeat to select more than one. Unknown IDs fail
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<LANG>\fR
Force one grammar for a single extensionless file
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
python
.IP \(bu 2
javascript
.IP \(bu 2
typescript
.IP \(bu 2
tsx
.IP \(bu 2
rust
.IP \(bu 2
php
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-speculative\fR
Omit findings carrying speculative evidence
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Include evidence class and tier in human output
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\-skips\fR
Treat any skipped file or subtree as an incomplete scan and exit 2
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-language\fR \fI<REQUIRE_LANGUAGE>\fR
Require complete coverage of a language (repeatable, e.g. php or haskell)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
